<% content_for :title, "Turbo Disable With" %>
<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Forms</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Turbo Disable With</h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground">
    The submitting state for a Rails form: while a submission runs, every button marked
    <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">data-turbo-disable-with</code> is disabled, keeps its size and shows a loading state — text, a spinner or a
    pulse — and a screen reader hears it. It is restored when Turbo reports the response.
  </p>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Preview</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-6 p-12 mb-8">
  <%= form_with url: demo_submit_path do %>
    <%= render(Ui::ButtonComponent.new(type: "submit", data: { turbo_disable_with: "Saving...", turbo_disable_style: "text" })) { "Text style" } %>
  <% end %>
  <%= form_with url: demo_submit_path do %>
    <%= render(Ui::ButtonComponent.new(type: "submit", variant: :outline, data: { turbo_disable_with: "Saving...", turbo_disable_style: "spinner" })) { "Spinner style" } %>
  <% end %>
  <%= form_with url: demo_submit_path do %>
    <%= render(Ui::ButtonComponent.new(type: "submit", variant: :outline, data: { turbo_disable_with: "Saving...", turbo_disable_style: "pulse" })) { "Pulse style" } %>
  <% end %>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Rails' and Turbo's own versions</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  There are three attributes with nearly the same name. Use this one, and only this one, on a button:
</p>
<ul class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-2 mb-8 list-disc ps-5">
  <li><strong>Rails' <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">data-disable-with</code></strong> is what <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">f.submit</code> adds on its own. It is read by
      rails-ujs, which a Rails 7+ app no longer loads, so under Turbo it does nothing.</li>
  <li><strong>Turbo's <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">data-turbo-submits-with</code></strong> swaps the text of the button that submitted, for a
      Turbo-driven submission. Text only, that one button only.</li>
  <li><strong>The kit's <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">data-turbo-disable-with</code></strong> adds what those don't: the spinner and pulse styles at
      the button's own height; every marked button in the form, not only the one clicked; <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-busy</code> and a
      polite announcement; forms with <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">data-turbo="false"</code>, which Turbo never sees; restoring the button
      before Turbo caches the page and when the browser brings it back from its back-forward cache; and a default text that
      is translatable, <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">rails_ui_kit.turbo_disable_with.processing</code>.</li>
</ul>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-8">
  Don't combine it with <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">data-turbo-submits-with</code> on the same button: both rewrite its content, and they
  restore it at different moments.
</p>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Setup</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-3">Mount once in your layout:</p>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800 mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-neutral-400">Layout — ERB</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#disable-with-setup" class="text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="disable-with-setup" class="text-neutral-200"><%= h(example_disable_with_setup) %></code></pre>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Usage</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800 mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-neutral-400">ERB</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#disable-with-usage" class="text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="disable-with-usage" class="text-neutral-200"><%= h(example_disable_with_usage) %></code></pre>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Options</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Attribute</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <% [
        ["data-turbo-disable-with",          "Text to show while submitting. Defaults to 'Processing...' (or the meta global default)."],
        ["data-turbo-disable-style",          "Loading style: text (default), spinner (animated spinner), or pulse (fades the button)."],
        ["meta[turbo-disable-with-default]",  "Global fallback text for any button without an explicit data-turbo-disable-with value."],
      ].each do |attr, desc| %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary whitespace-nowrap"><%= attr %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= desc %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-8">
  No component renders the meta tag — you write it — so translate the fallback text with
  <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">I18n.t('rails_ui_kit.turbo_disable_with.processing')</code> as its <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">content:</code>; see
  <%= link_to "Internationalization", i18n_path, class: "underline" %>.
</p>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Accessibility</h2>
<ul class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-2 mb-8 list-disc ps-5">
  <li>Announces the loading state via an <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">aria-live="polite"</code> region so screen readers are notified.</li>
  <li>Re-enables and restores the original button text on <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">turbo:submit-end</code>.</li>
  <li>The button is <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-busy="true"</code> while it waits, and disabled, so it can't be pressed twice.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">When not to use it</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-8">
  A submission that finishes faster than a person can see doesn't need it, and a request that runs for more than a few
  seconds needs more than it: progress, or a job the page reports on. For a submit button rendered by
  <%= link_to "Button", button_path, class: "text-primary underline" %>, pass the attribute through <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">data:</code>.
</p>
